+---------------------------------
+-- Block name and description --
+---------------------------------
+-- Baseband-frame length enforcer, self-synchronising version.
+--
+-- The incoming AXI stream is expected to carry raw DVB-S2 transport data
+-- whose frames are delimited by a SYNC byte (0xB8) followed by a MODCOD
+-- configuration byte.  Internally the block:
+--
+--   1. Scans for SYNC (0xB8)
+--   2. Decodes the MODCOD byte -> constellation, code rate, frame type, pilots
+--   3. Looks up the matching Kbch frame length
+--   4. Emits exactly Kbch/8 data bytes with m_tlast on the last one
+--   5. Consumes any inter-frame padding, then searches for the next SYNC
+--
+-- The decoded configuration is encoded into m_tuser (tid) so that every
+-- downstream block sees the correct MODCOD sideband for the frame in flight.
+--
+-- The original axi_stream_frame_slicer in fpga_cores is left untouched;
+-- all DVB-specific logic lives here in the work library.
+
 ---------------
 -- Libraries --
 ---------------
